00:04:27.560 --> 00:04:29.720
There's a nuance here worth understanding

00:04:29.720 --> 00:04:32.740
when a client receives the signed environmental assessment

00:04:32.740 --> 00:04:36.840
certificate and immediately asks which parameters must be added

00:04:36.840 --> 00:04:39.340
to the existing groundwater monitoring network

00:04:39.340 --> 00:04:40.880
before construction begins.

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:44.860
The certificate references site-specific trigger levels

00:04:44.860 --> 00:04:49.100
rather than default CSR standards yet the project footprint

00:04:49.100 --> 00:04:52.540
overlaps an area with historical aggregate extraction

00:04:52.540 --> 00:04:55.180
that may already contain elevated metals.

00:04:56.040 --> 00:04:59.600
Experience practitioners recognize that the certificate conditions

00:04:59.600 --> 00:05:03.040
often require quarterly sampling for the first two years

00:05:03.040 --> 00:05:05.860
with statistical analysis against background

00:05:05.860 --> 00:05:07.740
rather than generic guidelines.

00:05:08.740 --> 00:05:11.520
They request the full certificate schedule of conditions

00:05:11.520 --> 00:05:13.880
before finalizing the sampling plan.

00:05:14.380 --> 00:05:17.680
The key insight is that certificate conditions frequently

00:05:17.680 --> 00:05:20.520
tighten the temporal resolution of monitoring

00:05:20.520 --> 00:05:23.640
compared with CSR protocol for requirements,

00:05:24.100 --> 00:05:27.140
particularly for parameters linked to silica processing,

00:05:27.560 --> 00:05:29.420
such as turbidity and pH.

00:05:30.420 --> 00:05:32.860
The mistake I see most often is assuming

00:05:32.860 --> 00:05:37.120
the certificate simply layers on top of existing CSR obligations

00:05:37.120 --> 00:05:40.320
without reconciling differing statistical approaches

00:05:40.320 --> 00:05:41.780
or sampling frequencies.

00:05:42.420 --> 00:05:45.040
The fix is to map each certificate condition

00:05:45.040 --> 00:05:48.700
against the applicable CSR protocol within the first week

00:05:48.700 --> 00:05:50.940
of receipt and document any conflicts

00:05:50.940 --> 00:05:52.700
for early regulator discussion.

